one of my favorite youtube channels is  quinn's ideas  i can hardly remember there was a time  when i didn't watch it  quinn's idea started out recovering  mostly dune with some game of thrones  mixed in but in the last two years he  has broadened his coverage to also  include foundation hyperion and the  works of hp lovecraft  thus it appears quinn and iya have  everything in common  so it didn't come as a surprise he  started his own fiction project the  fantasy comic tajia  while i'm relatively new to reading  comics thanks to quinn i have delved  into neil gaiman's the sandman and  jodorowsky's the in-cal  now after two years what started as an  indiegogo project has finally been  completed with the first volume tadya  exordium being released to backers  and this is a review of the digital  version  while watching quinn's dune videos you  quickly get the impression that the  all-female ben and jesuit are amongst  his favorite characters in frank  herbert's fictional universe  they are certainly mine  that combined with some other influences  ensures tadia would be about witches and  witchcraft  but before i analyze tatya in detail let  me describe what it is about  tarya starts when two witches approach  lord stefan in the night about the  bargain they have struck decades back  in favor of being lifted lifted out of  poverty and into the nobility stefron  would give the witches his eldest  daughter as you may guess  stefan is not keen to honor the bargain  but unlike other instances of this trope  he is not stupid either  the witches command him to leave his  home unguarded  this leaves the witches of hekate an  opportunity to impregnate his eldest  daughter using magical means  from which tadya is born  the headstrong child appears fascinated  with the old legends of the witches and  the ancient enemy baelor  the latter is on the rise but can only  send fragments of himself into the realm  they are called fomori  these are capable of possessing humans  and are responsible of a number of  murders  tadia and her new chambermaid ethita  decide to stop them  while ultimately successful by the end  of exordium it is discovered that the  witches of hikari allowed one of them  for boys to pass from otherworld to this  realm in order to activate taijia's  special powers  their intentions for this remains  unknown  what struck me first and foremost about  tadia is how quinn has created a fully  fleshed out fictional universe with its  own rules and rituals  this path can be both fun to do for any  author but also hard to get right  i know how it can be done from the  method described by arthur arson scott  card from his non-fiction book how to  write science fiction and fantasy  queen stadia feels like this as if it is  one of the better thought out fictional  worlds  tidia exodium is ripe with many  influences from popular culture as  mentioned there is a fair amount of  inspiration from the banerjester's  sisters from dune in the sisters of  hegarty  their powers and independence being too  noteworthy  but i also see influences from  cinderella especially with tardies  difficult relationship with her mother a  stepmother i must say  the evil named bailor and this femorian  stem from irish mythology  dungeons and dragons also has an evil  named balor although i am not certain  if quinn was influenced by it  finally there are parallels to the  sandman comics by neil gaiman  there is a similar importance to the  dream world  there are also familiar tropes within  tadia  the sisters of hekate are witches who  live in the forest  their lives and power are underfed from  a new religion whose god is  whose god is referred to as the father  with its own bible called the holy tone  thus the feminine naturalist world is  threatened by the masculine artificial  world  one of the best parts of tadia exordium  is the artwork  the drawings made by matthew belden  blends medieval realism with fantasy the  setting and characters have considerable  detail and a lot  and add a lot to the sense of immersion  this is topped off by the wonderful  color palette used by colorist jean  francois bolio  the dark blues of the night the glow of  the halves inside the room and the  amazing color explosions caused by magic  are unlike anything i've seen before  i am not certain how much both artists  have cooperated on this book but it  feels like they did  both styles enhance each other and the  story  tadya could have been a book  and it had been a book no doubt the  second volume would have already been  released  but this comic book is something special  yes i can see many influences within  tadia exordium  consciously or not  but i think talia succeeds on its own  just as well  while i would have loved it while i  would have loved it to be a longer comic  book it is surprisingly effective as an  introduction or beginning which is what  exordium actually means  tatia's journey in the story is a  complete one as she battles the forces  of balor  there's even a lengthy prologue that  reminds me a lot of the sandman comics  with its theme of betrayal and broken  promises  exodium is such a self-contained story  while a cliffhanger is present it does  not dominate  i hope quinn will manage to continue  this series  i think exordium is a labor of love that  lasted almost three years  no doubt a second book  should be produced more quickly  i understand there are some production  difficult difficulties culminating in a  change of letter  i think that haste  is the cause of one or two typos but  they are not a big deal  i hope i will get my hardback copies  soon  tadia exodium was not meant to be read  from a computer screen  check out the link in the description  for the indiegogo page for tardia  also don't forget to check out quinn's  channel  finally if you've if you have enjoyed  this video then please click the like  button  if you want more content like it then  please hit the subscribe button that  will help my channel grow
 

